# Reference .bazelrc for dap_modules -- see ../../README.md, in particular
# "Required .bazelrc configs" and "Remote deployment over SSH".
#
# `gdbnf` and `debugpy` here are deliberately the exact names, ports, and
# `run_under` shape dap_modules.project already assumes by default (see
# project.lua). Nothing in .nvim-dap.lua needs to change to use them; it's
# included in this example only to make the schema explicit. Larger
# Bazel monorepos in this space (flight-software / robotics) commonly use
# these same two names already -- see this directory's README.md
# "Compatibility" section.

# C++ / Rust: build with full debug info, then run under gdbserver bound to
# a fixed local port so a locally-run gdb can attach to it.
build:gdbnf --compilation_mode=dbg
build:gdbnf --copt=-fno-omit-frame-pointer
build:gdbnf --strip=never
run:gdbnf --run_under="gdbserver :1234"

# Python: run under debugpy, paused until Neovim attaches.
build:debugpy --compilation_mode=dbg
run:debugpy --run_under="python3 -m debugpy --listen 0.0.0.0:5678 --wait-for-client"

# Remote deployment over SSH (dap_modules/remote.lua) -- cross-compile only:
# no `run_under` here, since remote.lua starts gdbserver itself once the
# binary has been rsynced to the target. Uncomment and point
# --platforms/--extra_toolchains at your own registered cross-toolchain to
# use <leader>bH / :DapRemoteDebug against a real board.
#
# build:remote-arm64 --platforms=//platforms:arm64-linux
# build:remote-arm64 --compilation_mode=dbg
# build:remote-arm64 --copt=-fno-omit-frame-pointer
# build:remote-arm64 --strip=never
